course: dictionary
lesson: 3063
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the words around them show which meaning is meant. Economically is one of these words. It can be about money, trade, jobs and business, as in a country that grows economically. It can also mean using very little, without waste, as in using water economically.
explain: Look for the clues. «Economically disadvantaged» is about being poor, so the phrase is about money. Cutting paper economically means cutting it so that none is wasted, so the meaning here is about using less.
explain: Use the swap check. Put your meaning into the sentence in place of the hard word. If "about money and jobs" or "using little, without waste" still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
fact: Economically means in a way that is about money, trade, jobs and business.
fact: Economically also means without wasting money, time or materials; using little.
fact: «Economically inactive» means not working and not looking for work.
fact: «Economically disadvantaged» means poor.
fact: Phrases you may meet include economically developed, economically important and live economically.
exercise: The town grew economically after the new factory opened. What does economically mean here? | Very slowly and quietly | *In a way about money, trade and jobs | By walking everywhere | Without wasting any paper
exercise: Mia tries to use water economically when she brushes her teeth. What does it mean? | Wasting as much water as she can | *Using little water, without waste | Drinking all the water up | Singing loudly to the tap
exercise: «Economically inactive» means what? | Being a great inventor | Working very hard every day | *Not working and not looking for work | Living by the sea
test: The school asked families to use lights economically. What does it mean? | *Using only what is needed, so no energy is wasted | Painting them bright colours | Leaving them on all day | Breaking them to see inside
test: Which sentence uses economically to mean about money and business? | *The country's trade grew economically last year | He sang economically all night | The cat sat economically in the sun | She ate her soup economically with a spoon
exam: Which meaning fits best in «a bridge that is economically important to the town»? | Very old and falling down | *Important for money, trade and jobs | Made of paper and easy to fold | Cheap and quick to walk over
